{"id":1217,"date":"2015-05-17T20:48:26","date_gmt":"2015-05-17T20:48:26","guid":{"rendered":"http:\/\/www.swat4ls.org\/?page_id=1217"},"modified":"2016-08-15T13:45:00","modified_gmt":"2016-08-15T13:45:00","slug":"useful-info","status":"publish","type":"page","link":"https:\/\/www.swat4ls.org\/workshops\/cambridge2015\/useful-info\/","title":{"rendered":"Useful Info"},"content":{"rendered":"<h3>Shortcut to Clare College for Tutorials and Conference<\/h3>\n<p>We have added an <strong>important shortcut<\/strong> route to the <a title=\"Venue\" href=\"https:\/\/www.swat4ls.org\/workshops\/cambridge2015\/venue\/\">venue page<\/a> &#8211; please see this for information. This will allow you to take a quick route from the city centre to <a href=\"http:\/\/clareconferencing.com\/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Clare College Conferencing<\/a>\u00a0where the event is being held.<\/p>\n<h3>Travel to Cambridge<\/h3>\n<p>By Air: The closest major airport is Stansted which serves many routes to Europe and is about a <a href=\"http:\/\/www.thetrainline.com\/train-times\/stansted-airport-to-cambridge-station\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">35 minute train ride<\/a> or 40 minutes drive to\u00a0Cambridge. There are <a href=\"http:\/\/www.nationalexpress.com\/coach\/Landing\/route.aspx?to=Cambridge&amp;from=Stansted&amp;gclid=Cj0KEQjwsb-vBRCLj7TvqpGx_MoBEiQALgFGnt4xyqAMh1dEXB_Ai6BIoEXNcCnJPWOmusXTZCOa24caAi3s8P8HAQ&amp;utm_source=google&amp;utm_medium=cpc&amp;utm_term=+stansted%20+to%20+cambridge&amp;utm_content=K_CREATIVE_HEADLINE&amp;utm_campaign=UK|EN|GO|GEN|BM|Stansted%20to%20Cambridge\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">also buses<\/a> which depart from the city centre\u00a0and take around 50 minutes. Heathrow and Gatwick airports (and to a lesser extend London Luton) are\u00a0extremely well connected internationally. Getting to Cambridge is a longer affair though and requires either a 90 minute car journey or trains connecting through London. The website\u00a0<a href=\"http:\/\/www.thetrainline.com\/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">thetrainline.com<\/a>\u00a0can help plan your journey.<\/p>\n<h3>Parking at\u00a0Clare College Conferncing and EBI<\/h3>\n<p>There will be a very limited number of parking spaces for the first 3 days at Clare College Conferencing. If you wish to park a car please let us know as soon as possible by emailing me &lt;james@factbio.com&gt; Parking at EBI is possible, but again we require advanced notice (email me) as you will need a permit.<\/p>\n<h3>Cambridge Accommodation<\/h3>\n<p>Cambridge has a range of hotels on offer though booking up early is recommended as it is a popular city for tourists over the Christmas period. Below is a selection of hotels, ordered by proximity\u00a0to Clare College Conferencing and with a link to the TripAdvisor review. It is often possible to get a lower\u00a0price using a third party website such as <a href=\"http:\/\/www.expedia.co.uk\/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Expedia<\/a> or <a href=\"http:\/\/www.trivago.co.uk\/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Trivago<\/a> so look around! The cheapest tend to be the Travelodge and Premier Inn hotels (end of this list).<\/p>\n<p><a href=\"http:\/\/www.cambridgecityhotel.co.uk\/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Cambridge City Hotel<\/a>\u00a0&#8211; 0.6 miles from venue (12 minute walk)<br \/>\n<a href=\"http:\/\/www.tripadvisor.co.uk\/Hotel_Review-g186225-d189358-Reviews-Cambridge_City_Hotel-Cambridge_Cambridgeshire_England.html\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">TripAdvisor review<\/a><\/p>\n<p><a href=\"http:\/\/www.regencyguesthouse.co.uk\/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Regency Guest House\u00a0Cambridge<\/a> &#8211; 0.8 miles from venue<br \/>\n<a href=\"http:\/\/www.tripadvisor.co.uk\/Hotel_Review-g186225-d214733-Reviews-Regency_Guest_House-Cambridge_Cambridgeshire_England.html\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">TripAdvisor review<\/a><\/p>\n<p><a href=\"http:\/\/www.regenthotel.co.uk\/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Regent Hotel Cambridge<\/a> &#8211; 0.8 miles from venue<br \/>\n<a href=\"http:\/\/www.tripadvisor.co.uk\/Hotel_Review-g186225-d211008-Reviews-Regent_Hotel-Cambridge_Cambridgeshire_England.html\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">TripAdvisor review<\/a><\/p>\n<p><a href=\"http:\/\/www.lensfieldhotel.co.uk\/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">\u00a0The Lensfield<\/a> &#8211; 0.9 miles from venue<br \/>\n<a href=\"http:\/\/www.tripadvisor.co.uk\/Hotel_Review-g186225-d193383-Reviews-The_Lensfield-Cambridge_Cambridgeshire_England.html\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">TripAdvisor review<\/a><\/p>\n<p><a href=\"http:\/\/www.gonvillehotel.co.uk\/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">The Gonville Hotel<\/a>\u00a0&#8211; 1 mile from venue<br \/>\n<a href=\"http:\/\/www.tripadvisor.co.uk\/Hotel_Review-g186225-d192791-Reviews-The_Gonville_Hotel-Cambridge_Cambridgeshire_England.html\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">TripAdvisor review<\/a><\/p>\n<p><a href=\"http:\/\/www.arundelhousehotels.co.uk\/cambridge\/index.php\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Arundel House Hotel, Cambridge<\/a> &#8211; 1 mile from venue<br \/>\n<a href=\"http:\/\/www.tripadvisor.co.uk\/Hotel_Review-g186225-d210084-Reviews-Arundel_House_Hotel-Cambridge_Cambridgeshire_England.html\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">TripAdvisor review<\/a><\/p>\n<p><a href=\"http:\/\/www.sjhotels.co.uk\/cambridge\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Royal Cambridge Hotel<\/a> &#8211; 1 mile from venue<br \/>\n<a href=\"http:\/\/www.tripadvisor.co.uk\/Hotel_Review-g186225-d191756-Reviews-Royal_Cambridge_Hotel-Cambridge_Cambridgeshire_England.html\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">TripAdvisor review<\/a><\/p>\n<p><a href=\"https:\/\/www.travelodge.co.uk\/hotels\/577\/Cambridge-Newmarket-Road-hotel\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Travelodge Cambridge Newmarket Road<\/a> &#8211; 1.4 miles from venue<br \/>\n<a href=\"http:\/\/www.tripadvisor.co.uk\/Hotel_Review-g186225-d4419705-Reviews-Travelodge_Newmarket_Road_Cambridge-Cambridge_Cambridgeshire_England.html\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">TripAdvisor review<\/a><\/p>\n<p><a href=\"http:\/\/www.premierinn.com\/en\/hotel\/CAMNEW\/cambridge-city-east\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Premier Inn Cambridge City East<\/a>\u00a0&#8211; 1.5 miles from venue<br \/>\n<a href=\"http:\/\/www.tripadvisor.co.uk\/Hotel_Review-g186225-d7193220-Reviews-Premier_Inn_Cambridge_City_East-Cambridge_Cambridgeshire_England.html\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">TripAdvisor review<\/a><\/p>\n<p><a href=\"https:\/\/www.travelodge.co.uk\/hotels\/255\/Cambridge-Central-hotel\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Travelodge Cambridge Central<\/a> &#8211; 1.7 miles from venue (35 minute walk)<br \/>\n<a href=\"http:\/\/www.tripadvisor.co.uk\/Hotel_Review-g186225-d446834-Reviews-Travelodge_Cambridge_Central-Cambridge_Cambridgeshire_England.html\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">TripAdvisor review<\/a><\/p>\n<h3>Visiting\u00a0Cambridge<\/h3>\n<p>Cambridge is a city steeped in history and home to some of the oldest Universities in the world. The <a href=\"http:\/\/www.visitcambridge.org\/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Visit Cambridge<\/a> website has links to events and activities taking place over December.<\/p>\n<p>As Cambridge is not a big city, <a href=\"http:\/\/www.visitcambridge.org\/official-tours\/official-public-daily-walking-tours-of-cambridge\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">the walking tours<\/a> are very popular and worth considering if you have some free time.<\/p>\n<p>Punting along the city&#8217;s River Cam is a very popular activity for locals and tourists alike (yes even during the winter). There is usually no need to book punting in advance and you can find many available by taking a short walk to <a href=\"http:\/\/www.scudamores.com\/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Scudamores<\/a>\u00a0(<a href=\"https:\/\/www.google.co.uk\/maps\/place\/Scudamore&#039;s+Punting+Cambridge\/@52.2011682,0.1163095,18z\/data=!4m5!1m2!2m1!1spunting+cambridge!3m1!1s0x0000000000000000:0xf4ca551a0da78cb7\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">google map link<\/a>).<\/p>\n<p>The <a href=\"http:\/\/www.fitzmuseum.cam.ac.uk\/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Fitzwilliam Museum<\/a> is the\u00a0arts and antiquities museum of the University of Cambridge\u00a0and\u00a0has been described as one of the greatest art collections of the UK.<\/p>\n<p>There are many <a href=\"http:\/\/www.tripadvisor.co.uk\/Restaurants-g186225-Cambridge_Cambridgeshire_England.html\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">good restaurants in Cambridge<\/a>. Some to consider:<\/p>\n<p><a href=\"http:\/\/www.cambscuisine.com\/cambridge-chop-house\/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">The Chop House<\/a><\/p>\n<p><a href=\"http:\/\/www.smokeworks.co.uk\/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Smokeworks<\/a><\/p>\n<p><a href=\"http:\/\/www.cottocambridge.co.uk\/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Cotto<\/a><\/p>\n<p><a href=\"http:\/\/www.theoakbistro.co.uk\/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">The Oak Bistro<\/a><\/p>\n<p>If you are feeling extravagant, there are two Michelin Star restaurants in Cambridge city centre:<\/p>\n<p><a href=\"http:\/\/www.midsummerhouse.co.uk\/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Midsummer House<\/a>\u00a0(**)<\/p>\n<p><a href=\"http:\/\/www.restaurantalimentum.co.uk\/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Alimentum<\/a>\u00a0(*)<\/p>\n","protected":false},"excerpt":{"rendered":"<p>Shortcut to Clare College for Tutorials and Conference We have added an important shortcut route to the venue page &#8211; please see this for information. This will allow you to take a quick route from the city centre to Clare &hellip; <a href=\"https:\/\/www.swat4ls.org\/workshops\/cambridge2015\/useful-info\/\">Continue reading <span class=\"meta-nav\">&rarr;<\/span><\/a><\/p>\n","protected":false},"author":1,"featured_media":1853,"parent":1136,"menu_order":0,"comment_sta